      // What a copy made with the team code may do
      'mem.btn': 'What a player copy and a coach copy can do',
      'mem.title': 'What a player copy and a coach copy can do',
      'mem.intro': 'The sharing rules decide what a player can see. This decides what they can do with it, and which modules are even on their menu. It is saved with the shared file, so every device that joins with the code opens this way.',
      'mem.readOnly': 'Players open the app read-only',
      'mem.readOnlyHint': 'Every button that would add, change or delete something is taken off their screen, and the app refuses the change even if one is reached another way. It only applies to a device whose role is Player and that follows your file \u2014 your own copy and your coaches are untouched.',
      'mem.training': 'Except {0}',
      'mem.trainingHint': 'They may plan their own sessions, add their own drills and log their own records. What you made stays as it is \u2014 they cannot change or delete the club\u2019s library, only their own work.',
      'mem.modules': 'Modules they can see',
      'mem.modulesHint': 'Untick a module and it is gone from their sidebar. Nothing is deleted, and it is back the moment you tick it again.',
      'mem.modMin': 'Only what a player needs',
      'mem.coachModules': 'Areas a squad coach can open',
      'mem.coachModulesHint': 'For a coach who joined with one squad\u2019s own password. They already see nothing but that squad \u2014 this decides which areas of it they get: matches, the event planner, live scouting, the board, reports and the rest. It is the starting point for every squad; give one squad a different set with Areas next to its coach word under Role passwords. A coach holding the club-wide word is not touched by this.',
      'mem.coachModMin': 'Only what a squad coach needs',
      'mem.coachAreas': 'Areas',
      'mem.coachAreasTitle': 'Areas for {0}',
      'mem.coachAreasIntro': 'Tick what this squad\u2019s coach can open once they join with the word beside it. Untick a module and it is gone from their sidebar \u2014 nothing is deleted, and it is back the moment you tick it again.',
      'mem.note': 'This reaches the players on their next sync, so you can tighten or loosen it at any time without handing out a new code.',
      'mem.saved': 'Player copy saved',
      'mem.stateFull': 'Players: full access',
      'mem.stateRead': 'Players: read-only \u00b7 {0} of {1} modules',
      'mem.badge': 'Read-only',
      'mem.blocked': 'This is a read-only team copy. Ask your coach if something needs changing.',
      'mem.roleLocked': 'A read-only team copy cannot change its own role. Ask a coach to change it, or leave the shared database below.',
      // Role passwords — the word that decides what a joining device may be
      'rk.btn': 'Role passwords',
      'rk.title': 'Role passwords',
      'rk.intro': 'The team code says which database. One of these words says what the device that pasted it is allowed to be. Send each person their code and the word for their role — they type both once, on the screen where they join.',
      'rk.warn': 'Only a scrambled form of these words is stored, so this screen is the only place they can be read. Write them down somewhere safe: they cannot be recovered, only replaced.',
      'rk.codeNote': 'The team code carries the scrambled form with it, so a player is checked the moment they paste it \u2014 no sync needed. Make a new set and the old code stops accepting the old words, so hand the code out again with them.',
      'rk.note': 'A device that joins without a word, or with one that does not match, comes in as a player — which is the read-only copy if you switched that on.',
      'rk.storeHint': 'Whoever holds the Super Admin word can do everything on their own copy, so hand that one out like a key to the club office.',
      'rk.on': 'Role passwords: on', 'rk.off': 'Role passwords: not made yet',
      'rk.make': 'Make the passwords', 'rk.again': 'New passwords',
      'rk.againAsk': 'Make new passwords? The ones you handed out stop working, and everybody who has not joined yet needs the new one.',
      'rk.made': 'Role passwords made',
